## Handling Browser Dialogs

Browsers can show three types of dialogs: **alert**, **confirm**, and **prompt**.

### Alert Dialogs

```typescript
// Set up listener BEFORE triggering the alert
page.on(''dialog'', async dialog => {
  console.log(dialog.message()); // Get alert message
  await dialog.accept(); // Close the alert
});

// Trigger action that shows alert
await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Show Alert'' }).click();
```

### Confirm Dialogs (OK/Cancel)

```typescript
// Accept confirm dialog (click OK)
page.on(''dialog'', async dialog => {
  console.log(''Confirm message:'', dialog.message());
  await dialog.accept(); // Click OK
});

await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Delete'' }).click();

// Dismiss confirm dialog (click Cancel)
page.once(''dialog'', async dialog => {
  await dialog.dismiss(); // Click Cancel
});

await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Delete'' }).click();
```

### Prompt Dialogs (Input Text)

```typescript
// Enter text in prompt
page.on(''dialog'', async dialog => {
  console.log(''Prompt:'', dialog.message());
  await dialog.accept(''John Doe''); // Enter text and click OK
});

await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Enter Name'' }).click();

// Dismiss prompt
page.once(''dialog'', async dialog => {
  await dialog.dismiss(); // Click Cancel
});
```

### Dialog Properties

```typescript
page.on(''dialog'', async dialog => {
  console.log(''Type:'', dialog.type());       // ''alert'', ''confirm'', or ''prompt''
  console.log(''Message:'', dialog.message()); // Dialog text
  console.log(''Default:'', dialog.defaultValue()); // Default prompt value

  await dialog.accept();
});
```

:::practice language=typescript | height=400px | title=Practice Dialog Handling
import { test, expect } from ''@playwright/test'';

test(''handle different dialogs'', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto(''https://example.com'');

  // Handle alert
  page.once(''dialog'', async dialog => {
    expect(dialog.type()).toBe(''alert'');
    expect(dialog.message()).toContain(''Success'');
    await dialog.accept();
  });
  await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Submit'' }).click();

  // Handle confirm (accept)
  page.once(''dialog'', async dialog => {
    expect(dialog.type()).toBe(''confirm'');
    await dialog.accept(); // Click OK
  });
  await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Delete'' }).click();

  // Handle confirm (dismiss)
  page.once(''dialog'', async dialog => {
    await dialog.dismiss(); // Click Cancel
  });
  await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Delete'' }).click();

  // Handle prompt
  page.once(''dialog'', async dialog => {
    expect(dialog.type()).toBe(''prompt'');
    await dialog.accept(''Test Name'');
  });
  await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Enter Name'' }).click();
});
:::

:::warning Important!
Always set up the dialog listener **BEFORE** triggering the action that shows the dialog!
:::

## Working with iframes

iframes are like mini web pages inside your main page.

### Basic iframe Interaction

```typescript
// Method 1: By name or ID
const frame = page.frame({ name: ''my-iframe'' });
const frame = page.frame({ url: /.*embed.*/ });

// Method 2: Using frameLocator (recommended)
const frameLocator = page.frameLocator(''iframe[name="my-iframe"]'');

// Interact with elements inside frame
await frameLocator.getByLabel(''Username'').fill(''user'');
await frameLocator.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Submit'' }).click();
```

### Multiple Nested iframes

```typescript
// Access nested iframe
const parentFrame = page.frameLocator(''#parent-iframe'');
const childFrame = parentFrame.frameLocator(''#child-iframe'');

await childFrame.getByLabel(''Email'').fill(''test@example.com'');
```

### Wait for iframe to Load

```typescript
// Wait for frame to be loaded
await page.waitForLoadState(''networkidle'');

// Or wait for specific element in frame
const frame = page.frameLocator(''iframe'');
await frame.getByRole(''heading'').waitFor();
```

### Real Example: YouTube Embed

```typescript
test(''interact with YouTube iframe'', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto(''https://example.com/video'');

  // Access YouTube iframe
  const youtubeFrame = page.frameLocator(''iframe[src*="youtube.com"]'');

  // Click play button
  await youtubeFrame.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Play'' }).click();

  // Verify video is playing
  await expect(youtubeFrame.locator(''.playing-indicator'')).toBeVisible();
});
```

:::practice language=typescript | height=350px | title=Practice iframe Handling
import { test, expect } from ''@playwright/test'';

test(''work with iframes'', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto(''https://example.com/iframe-demo'');

  // Access iframe by selector
  const loginFrame = page.frameLocator(''iframe[name="login"]'');

  // Fill form inside iframe
  await loginFrame.getByLabel(''Email'').fill(''user@example.com'');
  await loginFrame.getByLabel(''Password'').fill(''password123'');
  await loginFrame.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Sign In'' }).click();

  // Verify success inside iframe
  await expect(loginFrame.getByText(''Welcome back'')).toBeVisible();

  // Switch back to main page
  await expect(page.getByRole(''heading'')).toHaveText(''Dashboard'');
});
:::

## Multiple Tabs & Windows

### Opening New Tabs

```typescript
// Wait for new page/tab to open
const [newPage] = await Promise.all([
  page.context().waitForEvent(''page''), // Wait for new page
  page.getByRole(''link'', { name: ''Open in new tab'' }).click() // Trigger
]);

// Work with new tab
await newPage.waitForLoadState();
await expect(newPage).toHaveTitle(/About/);

// Close new tab
await newPage.close();
```

### Handling Multiple Tabs

```typescript
test(''work with multiple tabs'', async ({ page, context }) => {
  await page.goto(''https://example.com'');

  // Open link in new tab (Ctrl+Click)
  const [newTab] = await Promise.all([
    context.waitForEvent(''page''),
    page.getByRole(''link'', { name: ''Help'' }).click({ modifiers: [''Control''] })
  ]);

  // Switch to new tab
  await newTab.waitForLoadState();
  await expect(newTab).toHaveURL(/.*help.*/);

  // Work in new tab
  await newTab.getByLabel(''Search'').fill(''How to test'');

  // Switch back to original tab
  await page.bringToFront();
  await page.getByRole(''button'').click();

  // Close the new tab
  await newTab.close();

  // Continue with original tab
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/.*example.com.*/);
});
```

### Popup Windows

```typescript
// Handle popup window
const [popup] = await Promise.all([
  page.waitForEvent(''popup''),
  page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Open Popup'' }).click()
]);

// Work with popup
await popup.waitForLoadState();
await popup.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Accept'' }).click();

// Popup closes automatically or close manually
await popup.close();
```

## Multiple Browser Contexts

Contexts are like **incognito windows** - isolated from each other.

### Why Use Multiple Contexts?

- ✅ Test multi-user scenarios (admin + regular user)
- ✅ Test different sessions simultaneously
- ✅ Parallel testing with isolated state

### Creating Multiple Contexts

```typescript
import { test, expect, chromium } from ''@playwright/test'';

test(''multi-user scenario'', async ({ browser }) => {
  // Create admin context
  const adminContext = await browser.newContext();
  const adminPage = await adminContext.newPage();

  // Create user context
  const userContext = await browser.newContext();
  const userPage = await userContext.newPage();

  // Admin logs in
  await adminPage.goto(''https://example.com/admin'');
  await adminPage.getByLabel(''Email'').fill(''admin@example.com'');
  await adminPage.getByLabel(''Password'').fill(''admin123'');
  await adminPage.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Login'' }).click();

  // User logs in
  await userPage.goto(''https://example.com'');
  await userPage.getByLabel(''Email'').fill(''user@example.com'');
  await userPage.getByLabel(''Password'').fill(''user123'');
  await userPage.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Login'' }).click();

  // Admin creates something
  await adminPage.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''New Post'' }).click();
  await adminPage.getByLabel(''Title'').fill(''Test Post'');
  await adminPage.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Publish'' }).click();

  // User verifies they can see it
  await userPage.reload();
  await expect(userPage.getByText(''Test Post'')).toBeVisible();

  // Clean up
  await adminContext.close();
  await userContext.close();
});
```

### Context with Permissions

```typescript
// Create context with specific permissions
const context = await browser.newContext({
  permissions: [''geolocation'', ''notifications''],
  geolocation: { latitude: 59.95, longitude: 30.31667 },
  locale: ''en-GB'',
  timezoneId: ''Europe/Paris'',
});

const page = await context.newPage();
```

